" (https://raw.githubusercontent.com/zhang677/PTXBench/main/README.md)\nciteturn47view0 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: last month; Content type: text/plain; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"turn45view1\",\"lineno\":1}); Total lines: 226\nL0: # PTXBench\nL1: \nL2: [![Paper](https://img.shields.io/badge/arXiv-2608.17379-b31b1b.svg)](https://arxiv.org/pdf/2608.17379)\nL3: [![Blog Post](https://img.shields.io/badge/Blog-ptxbench.html-blue)](https://zhang677.github.io/blog_md/ptxbench.html)\nL4: [![HuggingFace](https://img.shields.io/badge/🤗-PTXBench-yellow)](https://huggingface.co/collections/Genghan/ptxbench-qwen36-27b-sft-series)\nL5: \nL6: PTXBench is an open-source environment for evaluating and building kernel agents that use architecture-specifc CUDA/PTX. It contains:\nL7: - **mini-ptx-agent**: the reusable agent, prompt, trajectory inspection, and\nL8:   benchmark implementation.\nL9: - **FIBServe**: a GPU profiling service derived from [FlashInfer-Bench](https://bench.flashinfer.ai/).\nL10: \nL11: 🚧 This repository is still under construction.\nL12: ## System overview\nL13: \nL14: ![PTXBench system diagram](assets/ptxbench-system.png)\nL15: ## Get a first result\nL16: \nL17: The smallest real PTXBench run asks one model to optimize one GEMM for three\nL18: turns. It needs:\nL19: \nL20: - an NVIDIA Hopper/H100-class FIBServe instance loaded with the\nL21:   [`AccRL/accrl-training`](https://huggingface.co/datasets/AccRL/accrl-training)\nL22:   FlashInfer Trace dataset;\nL23: - the `ptxbench-eval:dev` Docker image; and\nL24: - either an OpenAI-compatible Qwen endpoint or credentials for one of the\nL25:   hosted models supported by `mini-ptx-agent`.\nL26: \nL27: Set up the Python environment and evaluator image:\nL28: ```bash\nL29: uv sync --all-packages --group dev\nL30: docker build -f docker/Dockerfile.eval -t ptxbench-eval:dev .\nL31: ```\nL32: \nL33: Start FIBServe as described below, then select a model. For a Qwen endpoint,\nL34: the served ID must exactly match `MODEL_NAME`:\nL35: \nL36: ```bash\nL37: export MODEL_NAME=Qwen3.6-27B\nL38: export ACCRL_MODEL_HOST=localhost:30062\nL39: export SERVICE_URL=http://localhost:10000\nL40: \nL41: uv run ptxbench quickstart --check\nL42: uv run ptxbench quickstart --run\nL43: ```\nL44: \nL45: For example, a hosted OpenAI model can be used without\nL46: `ACCRL_MODEL_HOST`:\nL47: ```bash\nL48: export MODEL_NAME=GPT-5.4\nL49: export OPENAI_API_KEY=...\nL50: uv run ptxbench quickstart --run\nL51: ```\nL52: ### Triton quickstart\nL53: \nL54: The same quickstart can generate and evaluate Triton kernels through the\nL55: standard evaluator and FIBServe setup; no Triton-specific Docker image is\nL56: required. Pass `--language triton` to select the checked-in Hopper Triton\nL57: prompt and configuration:\nL58: \nL59: ```bash\nL60: uv run ptxbench quickstart --language triton --check\nL61: uv run ptxbench quickstart --language triton --run\nL62: ```\nL63: \nL64: CUDA remains the default when `--language` is omitted.\nL65: Every run leaves the full `trajectories/exp_000.json`, evaluator logs, and a\nL66: concise `quickstart-result.json` under\nL67: `data/eval_runs/quickstart-...-gemm/`. CUDA candidates are saved as\nL68: `exp_000/kernel.cu`, while Triton candidates are saved as\nL69: `exp_000/kernel.py`; correctness-passing versions are additionally saved under\nL70: `success/exp_000/` as `kernel_vN.cu` or `kernel_vN.py`, respectively. The\nL71: report deliberately distinguishes “the runner completed” from “the kernel was\nL72: correct” and “the 1.0x target was achieved.” mini-ptx-agent writes trajectories\nL73: in a JSON format compatible with mini-swe-agent and its trajectory tooling.\nL74: Reprint any run with:\nL75: ```bash\nL76: uv run ptxbench quickstart --report data/eval_runs/quickstart-...-gemm\nL77: ```\nL78: ## Local paths\nL79: \nL80: For local development, configure the project/data paths and the Compose\nL81: trace-set collection:\nL82: \nL83: ```bash\nL84: export PTXBENCH_ROOT=/home/ubuntu/PTXBench\nL85: export PTXBENCH_DATA_ROOT=\"$PTXBENCH_ROOT/data\"\nL86: export PTXBENCH_TRACESETS_ROOT=\"$PTXBENCH_ROOT/data/datasets\"\nL87: export DATASET_ROOTS=/workspace/trace-sets/accrl-training\nL88: export MINI_PTX_AGENT_ROOT=\"$PTXBENCH_ROOT/packages/mini-ptx-agent\"\nL89: ```\nL90: \nL91: `PTXBENCH_DATA_ROOT` may point at an existing directory to hold experiment artifacts.\nL92: `PTXBENCH_TRACESETS_ROOT` is a shared parent directory on the host. Each child\nL93: is a complete FlashInfer Trace dataset with its own `definitions/` and\nL94: `workloads/` directories. For example:\nL95: \nL96: ```text\nL97: $PTXBENCH_TRACESETS_ROOT/\nL98: ├── accrl-training/\nL99: │   ├── definitions/\nL100: │   └── workloads/\nL101: └── another-trace-set/\nL102:     ├── definitions/\nL103:     └── workloads/\nL104: ```\nL105: \nL106: Compose bind-mounts that parent directory read-only at `/workspace/trace-sets`:\nL107: ```text\nL108: host:      /home/ubuntu/PTXBench/data/datasets\nL109: container: /workspace/trace-sets\nL110: ```\nL111: \nL112: `DATASET_ROOTS` is always a colon-separated list selecting dataset directories\nL113: inside the mount; a single dataset is simply a one-item list. Compose uses the\nL114: shared parent because it cannot expand one environment variable into a variable\nL115: number of bind mounts.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nPTXBench/data at main · zhang677/PTXBench · GitHub (https://github.com/zhang677/PTXBench/tree/main/data)\nciteturn47view1 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: last month; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"turn45view2\",\"lineno\":165}); Total lines: 225\nL58:     * EXPLORE BY TOPIC\nL59:       * cite34†AI L60:       * cite35†Software Development L61:       * cite36†DevOps L62:       * cite37†Security L63:       * cite38†View all topics L64: \nL65:     * EXPLORE BY TYPE\nL66:       * cite39†Customer stories L67:       * cite40†Events & webinars L68:       * cite41†Ebooks & reports L69:       * cite42†Business insights L70:       * cite43†GitHub Skills†skills.github.com L71:     * SUPPORT & SERVICES\nL72:       * cite14†Documentation†docs.github.com L73:       * cite44†Customer support†support.github.com L74:       * cite45†Community forum L75:       * cite46†Trust center L76:       * cite47†Partners L77: \nL78: cite48†View all resources L79: \nL80:   * Open Source\nL81: \nL82:     * COMMUNITY\nL83:       * cite49†GitHub SponsorsFund open source developers L84:     * PROGRAMS\nL85:       * cite50†Security Lab†securitylab.github.com L86:       * cite51†Maintainer Community†maintainers.github.com L87:       * cite52†Accelerator L88:       * cite53†GitHub Stars†stars.github.com L89:       * cite54†Archive Program†archiveprogram.github.com L90: \nL91:     * REPOSITORIES\nL92:       * cite55†Topics L93:       * cite56†Trending L94:       * cite57†Collections L95: \nL96:   * Enterprise\nL97: \nL98:     * ENTERPRISE SOLUTIONS\nL99:       * cite19†Enterprise platformAI-powered developer platform L100:     * AVAILABLE ADD-ONS\nL101:       * cite10†GitHub Advanced SecurityEnterprise-grade security features L102:       * cite58†Copilot for BusinessEnterprise-grade AI features L103:       * cite59†Premium SupportEnterprise-grade 24/7 support L104: \nL105:   * cite60†Pricing L106: \nL107: Search`/`\nL108: \nL109: cite1†Sign in L110: \nL111: cite61†Sign up L112: \nL113: Appearance settings\nL114: You signed in with another tab or window. Reload to refresh your session. You signed out in another tab or window. Reload to refresh your session. You switched accounts on another tab or window. Reload to refresh your session. Dismiss alert\nL115: \nL116: cite62†zhang677 / cite63†PTXBench Public\nL117: \nL118:   * cite64†Notifications You must be signed in to change notification settings\nL119:   * cite64†Fork 0 L120:   * cite64†Star L121:   * cite63†Code L122:   * cite65†Issues 0 L123:   * cite66†Pull requests 0 L124:   * cite67†Actions L125:   * cite68†Projects L126:   * cite69†Security and quality 0 L127:   * cite70†Insights L128: \nL129: Additional navigation options\nL130: ## Files Expand file tree\nL131: \nL132: main\nL133: \nL134: ## Breadcrumbs\nL135: \nL136:   1. cite71†PTXBench L137: \nL138: /\nL139: \nL140: # data\nL141: \nL142: /\nL143: \nL144: Copy path\nL145: \nL146: ## Directory actions\nL147: \nL148: [Input: Go to file]\nL149: \nL150: ## More options\nL151: \nL152: More options\nL153: \nL154: ## Directory actions\nL155: \nL156: ## More options\nL157: \nL158: More options\nL159: \nL160: ## Latest commit\nL161: \nL162: \nL163: \nL164: ## History\nL165: \nL166: History\nL167: \nL168: main\nL169: \nL170: ## Breadcrumbs\nL171: \nL172:   1. cite71†PTXBench L173: \nL174: /\nL175: \nL176: # data\nL177: \nL178: /\nL179: \nL180: Copy path\nL181: \nL182: Top\nL183: \nL184: ## Folders and files\nL185: \nL186: Name  | Name  | Last commit message  | Last commit date\nL187: --- | --- | --- | ---\nL188: ### parent directory\nL189: \nL190: cite71†.. L191: cite72†datasets | cite72†datasets |    |\nL192: cite73†README.md | cite73†README.md |    |\nL193: \nL194: ## cite74†README.md L195: # PTXBench data\nL196: \nL197: This directory is intentionally not populated by the source repository.\nL198: \nL199:   * `datasets/` is the collection root mounted into FIBServe. Each child trace dataset listed in `DATASET_ROOTS` contains its own `definitions/` and `workloads/` directories.\nL200:   * `eval_runs/` holds mini-ptx-agent trajectories, plans, logs, and successful kernels.\nL201:   * `sft_experiments/` holds optional Fixit synthesis/training artifacts.\nL202: The two public workflows expect:\nL203: \nL204:     `sft_experiments/\nL205:       test-fixit-qwen36-27b-gemini-glm/             Fixit input/output project\nL206:       mha-8def-single-turn-qwen36-27b-gemini-glm/   KernelGen input/output project\nL207:     eval_runs/                                      referenced trajectories/kernels\nL208:     `\nL209: Authorized users can retrieve the published s0-s6 training parquets from the private cite75†`Genghan/PTXBench-Qwen3.6-27B-SFT`†huggingface.co repository. Otherwise, set `PTXBENCH_DATA_ROOT` to an existing compatible data tree. Source preflight and data-closure validation are intentionally separate.\nL210: Release maintainers can export the historical Fixit source inputs without preserving machine-specific paths:\nL211: \nL212:     python scripts/build_fixit_data_bundle.py \\\nL213:       --pairs-csv /path/to/fixit-v5-gemini-kernel-pairs.csv \\\nL214:       --data-root /path/to/AccRL-exps \\\nL215:       --mini-agent-root /path/to/AccRL \\\nL216:       --output dist/fixit-source-data.tar.gz\nL217: The KernelGen source runs have a separate deterministic exporter:\nL218: \nL219:     python scripts/build_kernelgen_data_bundle.py \\\nL220:       --data-root /path/to/AccRL-exps \\\nL221:       --mini-agent-root /path/to/AccRL \\\nL222:       --output dist/kernelgen-source-data.tar.gz\nL223: \nL224: You can’t perform that action at this time.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n (https://raw.githubusercontent.com/zhang677/PTXBench/main/README.md)\nciteturn47view2 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: last month; Content type: text/plain; Source: find({\"ref_id\":\"turn45view1\",\"pattern\":\"AccRL\"}); Total lines: 226\nL0: # PTXBench\nL1: \nL2: [![Paper](https://img.shields.io/badge/arXiv-2608.17379-b31b1b.svg)](https://arxiv.org/pdf/2608.17379)\nL3: [![Blog Post](https://img.shields.io/badge/Blog-ptxbench.html-blue)](https://zhang677.github.io/blog_md/ptxbench.html)\nL4: [![HuggingFace](https://img.shields.io/badge/🤗-PTXBench-yellow)](https://huggingface.co/collections/Genghan/ptxbench-qwen36-27b-sft-series)\nL5: \nL6: PTXBench is an open-source environment for evaluating and building kernel agents that use architecture-specifc CUDA/PTX. It contains:\nL7: - **mini-ptx-agent**: the reusable agent, prompt, trajectory inspection, and\nL8:   benchmark implementation.\nL9: - **FIBServe**: a GPU profiling service derived from [FlashInfer-Bench](https://bench.flashinfer.ai/).\nL10: \nL11: 🚧 This repository is still under construction.\nL12: ## System overview\nL13: \nL14: ![PTXBench system diagram](assets/ptxbench-system.png)\nL15: ## Get a first result\nL16: \nL17: The smallest real PTXBench run asks one model to optimize one GEMM for three\nL18: turns. It needs:\nL19: \nL20: - an NVIDIA Hopper/H100-class FIBServe instance loaded with the\nL21:   [`AccRL/accrl-training`](https://huggingface.co/datasets/AccRL/accrl-training)\nL22:   FlashInfer Trace dataset;\nL23: - the `ptxbench-eval:dev` Docker image; and\nL24: - either an OpenAI-compatible Qwen endpoint or credentials for one of the\nL25:   hosted models supported by `mini-ptx-agent`.\nL26: \nL27: Set up the Python environment and evaluator image:\nL28: ```bash\nL29: uv sync --all-packages --group dev\nL30: docker build -f docker/Dockerfile.eval -t ptxbench-eval:dev .\nL31: ```\nL32: \nL33: Start FIBServe as described below, then select a model. For a Qwen endpoint,\nL34: the served ID must exactly match `MODEL_NAME`:\nL35: \nL36: ```bash\nL37: export MODEL_NAME=Qwen3.6-27B\nL38: export ACCRL_MODEL_HOST=localhost:30062\nL39: export SERVICE_URL=http://localhost:10000\nL40: \nL41: uv run ptxbench quickstart --check\nL42: uv run ptxbench quickstart --run\nL43: ```\nL44: \nL45: For example, a hosted OpenAI model can be used without\nL46: `ACCRL_MODEL_HOST`:\nL47: ```bash\nL48: export MODEL_NAME=GPT-5.4\nL49: export OPENAI_API_KEY=...\nL50: uv run ptxbench quickstart --run\nL51: ```\nL52: ### Triton quickstart\nL53: \nL54: The same quickstart can generate and evaluate Triton kernels through the\nL55: standard evaluator and FIBServe setup; no Triton-specific Docker image is\nL56: required. Pass `--language triton` to select the checked-in Hopper Triton\nL57: prompt and configuration:\nL58: \nL59: ```bash\nL60: uv run ptxbench quickstart --language triton --check\nL61: uv run ptxbench quickstart --language triton --run\nL62: ```\nL63: \nL64: CUDA remains the default when `--language` is omitted.\nL65: Every run leaves the full `trajectories/exp_000.json`, evaluator logs, and a\nL66: concise `quickstart-result.json` under\nL67: `data/eval_runs/quickstart-...-gemm/`. CUDA candidates are saved as\nL68: `exp_000/kernel.cu`, while Triton candidates are saved as\nL69: `exp_000/kernel.py`; correctness-passing versions are additionally saved under\nL70: `success/exp_000/` as `kernel_vN.cu` or `kernel_vN.py`, respectively. The\nL71: report deliberately distinguishes “the runner completed” from “the kernel was\nL72: correct” and “the 1.0x target was achieved.” mini-ptx-agent writes trajectories\nL73: in a JSON format compatible with mini-swe-agent and its trajectory tooling.\nL74: Reprint any run with:\nL75: ```bash\nL76: uv run ptxbench quickstart --report data/eval_runs/quickstart-...-gemm\nL77: ```\nL78: ## Local paths\nL79: \nL80: For local development, configure the project/data paths and the Compose\nL81: trace-set collection:\nL82: \nL83: ```bash\nL84: export PTXBENCH_ROOT=/home/ubuntu/PTXBench\nL85: export PTXBENCH_DATA_ROOT=\"$PTXBENCH_ROOT/data\"\nL86: export PTXBENCH_TRACESETS_ROOT=\"$PTXBENCH_ROOT/data/datasets\"\nL87: export DATASET_ROOTS=/workspace/trace-sets/accrl-training\nL88: export MINI_PTX_AGENT_ROOT=\"$PTXBENCH_ROOT/packages/mini-ptx-agent\"\nL89: ```\nL90: \nL91: `PTXBENCH_DATA_ROOT` may point at an existing directory to hold experiment artifacts.\nL92: `PTXBENCH_TRACESETS_ROOT` is a shared parent directory on the host. Each child\nL93: is a complete FlashInfer Trace dataset with its own `definitions/` and\nL94: `workloads/` directories. For example:\nL95: \nL96: ```text\nL97: $PTXBENCH_TRACESETS_ROOT/\nL98: ├── accrl-training/\nL99: │   ├── definitions/\nL100: │   └── workloads/\nL101: └── another-trace-set/\nL102:     ├── definitions/\nL103:     └── workloads/\nL104: ```\nL105: \nL106: Compose bind-mounts that parent directory read-only at `/workspace/trace-sets`:\nL107: ```text\nL108: host:      /home/ubuntu/PTXBench/data/datasets\nL109: container: /workspace/trace-sets\nL110: ```\nL111: \nL112: `DATASET_ROOTS` is always a colon-separated list selecting dataset directories\nL113: inside the mount; a single dataset is simply a one-item list. Compose uses the\nL114: shared parent because it cannot expand one environment variable into a variable\nL115: number of bind mounts.\nL116: Download the quickstart trace set from\nL117: [`AccRL/accrl-training`](https://huggingface.co/datasets/AccRL/accrl-training)\nL118: into `$PTXBENCH_TRACESETS_ROOT/accrl-training`. To load another trace set,\nL119: place it alongside that directory and extend the list:\nL120: \nL121: ```bash\nL122: export DATASET_ROOTS=/workspace/trace-sets/accrl-training:/workspace/trace-sets/another-trace-set\nL123: ```\nL124: \nL125: No files are merged on disk, and no dataset is copied into a Docker image.\nL126: ## Development setup\nL127: \nL128: ```bash\nL129: uv sync --all-packages --group dev\nL130: ```\nL131: \nL132: Install the optional Tinker training stack when reproducing an AccRL training\nL133: run:\nL134: \nL135: ```bash\nL136: uv sync --all-packages --extra training --group dev\nL137: uv run python -c \"import tinker, tinker_cookbook\"\nL138: ```\nL139: \nL140: The training commands require a valid `TINKER_API_KEY`; keep it in the\nL141: environment or a local `.env` file, which is ignored by Git.\nL142: \nL143: Build the isolated kernel evaluator:\nL144: ```bash\nL145: docker build -f docker/Dockerfile.eval -t ptxbench-eval:dev .\nL146: ```\nL147: \nL148: Build and start FIBServe:\nL149: \nL150: ```bash\nL151: cp .env.example docker/.env\nL152: docker compose --env-file docker/.env -f docker/compose.yaml up --build fibserve\nL153: ```\nL154: The public experiment index starts at [`experiments/README.md`](experiments/README.md).\nL155: The source/data boundary and release procedure are documented in\nL156: [`RELEASING.md`](RELEASING.md).\nL157: For Fixit, use\nL158: [`experiments/fixit/README.md`](experiments/fixit/README.md) as the\nL159: single start page and `scripts/reproduce_fixit.sh` as the runnable entrypoint.\nL160: \nL161: Use `scripts/smoke_fixit.sh --check` for a non-mutating dependency and\nL162: configuration preflight.\nL163: Use `scripts/reproduce_fixit.sh --check` to validate the complete source\nL164: closure and `from-scratch` to run failure mining, Gemini repair, SFT, and the\nL165: paper's expert-guided evaluation in order. KernelGen starts at\nL166: [`experiments/kernelgen/README.md`](experiments/kernelgen/README.md) and uses\nL167: `scripts/reproduce_kernelgen.sh`. `ptxbench-inspect` remains part of the\nL168: supported CLI.\nL169: \nL170: For a live run, select a dedicated OpenAI-compatible model endpoint. PTXBench\nL171: does not default to a shared model serve:\nL172: ```bash\nL173: MODEL_NAME=Qwen3.6-27B \\\nL174: ACCRL_MODEL_HOST=localhost:30062 \\\nL175: SERVICE_URL=http://localhost:11000 \\\nL176: scripts/smoke_fixit.sh --run\nL177: ```\nL178: \nL179: To run the same orchestration from the agent container, set\nL180: `PTXBENCH_HOST_ROOT` to the checkout's absolute host path. The path is mounted\nL181: at the same location in the agent so sibling eval containers launched through\nL182: the Docker socket can mount trajectory workspaces correctly:\nL183: ```bash\nL184: export PTXBENCH_HOST_ROOT=\"$(pwd)\"\nL185: docker compose -f docker/compose.yaml run --rm \\\nL186:   --entrypoint bash agent scripts/smoke_fixit.sh --check\nL187: ```\nL188: ## Harbor\nL189: PTXBench includes [Harbor-compatible tasks](integrations/harbor/README.md) that\nL190: run on an unmodified Harbor checkout while using `ptxbench eval` and FIBServe\nL191: for compilation, sanitization, and H100 benchmarking. The agent creates its implementation\nL192: from scratch; before launching a run, the checked-in instruction can be\nL193: refreshed from the live FIBServe definition to keep its task encoding aligned\nL194: with AccRL. The integration guide covers image builds, prompt rendering, Harbor\nL195: launch options, and the resulting ATIF trajectory.\nL196: ## Huggingface\nL197: Other example datasets include non-4096 sequence-length attention workload records at [`Genghan/accrl-training-heavy`](https://huggingface.co/datasets/Genghan/accrl-training-heavy) and a more diverse [`flashinfer-ai/flashinfer-trace`](https://huggingface.co/datasets/flashinfer-ai/flashinfer-trace). The byte-exact historical s0-s6 training parquets are also retained in\nL198: [`Genghan/PTXBench-Qwen3.6-27B-SFT`](https://huggingface.co/datasets/Genghan/PTXBench-Qwen3.6-27B-SFT).\nL199: ## Major dependencies\nL200: - **mini-swe-agent 2.4.6**: an external, exactly pinned Python dependency used\nL201:   as the agent runtime and Docker environment abstraction.\nL202: - **tinker-cookbook**: an optional, locked dependency for reproducing the\nL203:   Tinker SFT training and checkpoint-export workflow.\nL204: ## Citation\nL205: \nL206: If you use PTXBench in your work, please cite the [paper](http://arxiv.org/abs/2608.17379):\nL207: ```bibtex\nL208: @misc{ptxbench2026,\nL209:   title = {{PTXBench}: Benchmark and Adapt {LLMs} for {GPU} Kernel Optimization with Architecture-specific {PTX}},\nL210:   author = {Genghan Zhang and Yixin Dong and Chengze Fan and Zhichen Zeng and Yueming Yuan and Shaowei Zhu and Kunle Olukotun},\nL211:   year = {2026},\nL212:   eprint = {2608.17379},\nL213:   archivePrefix = {arXiv},\nL214:   primaryClass = {cs.CL},\nL215:   url = {http://arxiv.org/abs/2608.17379},\nL216: }\nL217: ```\nL218: ## Licensing and provenance\nL219: \nL220: PTXBench and mini-ptx-agent are Apache-2.0. FIBServe is derived from\nL221: FlashInfer Bench and preserves its Apache-2.0 license and NOTICE. mini-swe-agent\nL222: is consumed under its MIT license and is not vendored into this repository.\nL223: tinker-cookbook is consumed under Apache-2.0 and is also not vendored. See\nL224: [`NOTICE`](NOTICE) for the NVIDIA reference-material rationale, hosted-model\nL225: workflow terms, and licenses for code adapted from Helion and FlashAttention.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nPTXBench/data at main · zhang677/PTXBench · GitHub (https://github.com/zhang677/PTXBench/tree/main/data)\nciteturn47view3 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: last month; Content type: text/html; Source: find({\"ref_id\":\"turn45view2\",\"pattern\":\"json\"}); Total lines: 225\nNo matching text found for \"json\"--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nPTXBench/experiments at main · zhang677/PTXBench · GitHub (https://github.com/zhang677/PTXBench/tree/main/experiments)\nciteturn47view4 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: last month; Content type: text/html; Source: find({\"ref_id\":\"turn45view3\",\"pattern\":\"Name\"}); Total lines: 209\nL58:     * EXPLORE BY TOPIC\nL59:       * cite34†AI L60:       * cite35†Software Development L61:       * cite36†DevOps L62:       * cite37†Security L63:       * cite38†View all topics L64: \nL65:     * EXPLORE BY TYPE\nL66:       * cite39†Customer stories L67:       * cite40†Events & webinars L71:     * SUPPORT & SERVICES\nL72:       * cite14†Documentation†docs.github.com L73:       * cite44†Customer support†support.github.com L74:       * cite45†Community forum L75:       * cite46†Trust center L76:       * cite47†Partners L77: \nL78: cite48†View all resources L79: \nL80:   * Open Source\nL81: \nL82:     * COMMUNITY\nL83:       * cite49†GitHub SponsorsFund open source developers L84:     * PROGRAMS\nL85:       * cite50†Security Lab†securitylab.github.com L86:       * cite51†Maintainer Community†maintainers.github.com L87:       * cite52†Accel