161: \nL162: \nL163: \nL164: ## History\nL165: \nL166: History\nL167: \nL168: main\nL169: \nL170: ## Breadcrumbs\nL171: \nL172:   1. cite71†PTXBench L173: \nL174: /\nL175: \nL176: # experiments\nL177: \nL178: /\nL179: \nL180: Copy path\nL181: \nL182: Top\nL183: \nL184: ## Folders and files\nL185: \nL186: Name  | Name  | Last commit message  | Last commit date\nL187: --- | --- | --- | ---\nL188: ### parent directory\nL189: \nL190: cite71†.. L191: cite72†fixit | cite72†fixit |    |\nL192: cite73†kernelgen | cite73†kernelgen |    |\nL193: cite74†README.md | cite74†README.md |    |\nL194: \nL195: ## cite75†README.md L196: # Reproducible experiments\nL197: \nL198: This directory is the public experiment index. Runtime implementations live in the two packages, while each experiment directory contains only its ordered launchers and runnable instructions.\nL199: \nL200: Experiment  | Scope\nL201: --- | ---\nL202: cite76†Fixit | base-Qwen failure mining, Gemini repair, pair-reasoning synthesis, SFT, and expert-guided evaluation\nL203: cite77†KernelGen | correct-kernel collection, GLM-5.2 reasoning synthesis, the three-message SFT contract, and expert-guided evaluation\nL204: Large trajectories, kernels, reasoning JSONL, parquet, and checkpoints are published data artifacts rather than source files.\nL205: \nL206: Use `python scripts/build_fixit_data_bundle.py` to export the large, relocatable historical Fixit source-data archive separately from Git source. Use `python scripts/build_kernelgen_data_bundle.py` for the corresponding 12-run/521-row KernelGen source closure.\nL207: \nL208: You can’t perform that action at this time.\n"
